Description: Provides reproducible computational tools for occupational noise
    exposure assessment and spatial noise modelling. The package implements
    logarithmic sound-level addition, daily and weekly exposure calculations,
    noise dose and maximum admissible exposure time, hearing-protector
    calculations using APV, HML and SNR approaches, evaluation helpers aligned
    with the Spanish occupational-noise framework, free-field propagation,
    barrier-aware receiver calculations, spatial noise grids, noise contours,
    reverberation models and inverse estimation of source levels. A Shiny
    application is included for interactive occupational-noise calculations and
    mapping workflows while the calculation core remains independently callable
    and unit tested. User-facing messages and the interactive application support
    both Spanish and English through a shared internationalisation layer.
